  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe have a step function h:[0,2]\u2192[0,1] that satisfies \u222bh(x)dx=1, and we wish to minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx. The given initial solution achieves C\u2085=0.38085. To improve this, we will iterate with multiple resolutions (n_points) and apply a hybrid Bayesian optimization with local search. The key bottleneck is the optimization's difficulty in escaping local minima and the high dimensionality. We address this by combining stochastic global search (Bayesian optimization) with gradient-based refinement and multiple resolution transfers.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Representation: Piecewise constant function with n_points samples over [0,2]\n- Decision variables: h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f with sum(h)=n/2\n- Objective: minimize C\u2085 = (1/2) * max\u2096 |\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx| (continuous domain)\n- Discrete approximation: C\u2085 = max\u2096 corr_full[k] * dx (dx=2/n_points)\n- Feasibility conditions: 0\u2264h\u1d62\u22641 \u2200i, sum(h)=n/2\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Parent solution validation:\n- If 'initial_h_values' provided, up-convert to desired resolution while preserving sum and bounds\n- Else initialize with uniform random samples constrained to sum= n/2\n\nb) Core optimization loop:\n1. Bayesian optimization phase:\n   - Use Tree-structured Parzen Estimation (TPE) with EI acquisition function\n   - n_candidates = 20 (step size)\n   - Temperature schedule from 300 to 10 (log scale)\n   - Dimensionality adapts with increasing resolution\n\n2. Local refinement phase:\n   - 2-opt neighborhood search: modify two indices\n   - Maintain feasible points via clipping and repair\n   - Gradient-based refinement at low temperature\n\nc) Dimension transformation:\n- For n_points scaling:\n   - n_new = n_old * 2\u1d4f\n   - Interpolate parent solution if available, else randomize\n   - Constraint: dx decreases by factor 2\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\na) Bayesian TPE configuration:\n   - Prior: Gaussian process with RBF kernel\n   - Surrogates: Lower and upper bound approximations\n   - Failure tolerance: 3 restarts per temperature step\n\nb) 2-opt moves:\n   - Sample indices uniformly from [0,n]\n   - Generate mutant by flipping/interpolating values\n   - Adapt mutation rate to temperature\n\nc) Metadata-driven optimization:\n   - Track temperature, dimension, fitness\n   - Use Thompson sampling for exploration\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\na) Phase timing:\n   - Bayesian phase: 40% budget (\u2248440s)\n   - Refinement: 30% budget (\u2248330s)\n   - Local search: 20% budget (\u2248220s)\n   - Metadata: 10% budget (\u2248110s)\n\nb) Timeout handling:\n   - Save current best on timer interrupt\n   - Scale TPE parameters with remaining time\n\n6. Validation and return contract\na) Feasibility checks:\n   - Sum(h) must = n/2\n   - All entries in [0,1]\n   - C\u2085 = max(lin_corr[k]) * dx must be < current best\n\nb) Return format:\n(h_values (as_list), c5_bound, n_points)\nfeature: manual_adaptive = True",
